---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site.mjs';

const config = `{
  "mcpServers": {
    "specimen": {
      "command": "node",
      "args": ["/absolute/path/to/usespecimen/src/mcp.mjs"]
    }
  }
}`;
---

<Base
  title="MCP server — Specimen"
  description="Let a coding agent search and fetch verified DESIGN.md files without leaving the editor."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1 style="margin-top:2rem;">The MCP server</h1>
    <p>
      Exposes the registry to a coding agent over the Model Context Protocol, so
      it can find and fetch a design system without a browser and without you
      leaving the editor.
    </p>

    <h2>Install</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Not published to npm yet</strong>, so it runs from a clone. Requires
      Node 24.
    </p>
    <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/MrPiThon/usespecimen
cd usespecimen
npm install</code></pre>

    <p>Then point your MCP client at it:</p>
    <pre><code>{config}</code></pre>
    <p>
      The path must be absolute — an MCP client does not run the command from
      your project directory. To read from a registry other than
      <code>{SITE}</code>, set <code>SPECIMEN_REGISTRY</code> in the server's
      environment; there is no argv to pass one on.
    </p>

    <h2>Tools</h2>

    <h3><code>search_designs</code></h3>
    <p>
      Find a system by free text, or filter on facets taken straight from the
      extracted tokens.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>query</code> — matched against slug, name, brand and description</li>
      <li><code>polarity</code> — <code>light</code> or <code>dark</code>, the
        polarity of the default palette</li>
      <li><code>supportsDark</code> — only systems that respond to
        <code>prefers-color-scheme</code></li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Returns slugs, palettes and the date each system was verified. A search
      that matches nothing says what the registry does carry, so an agent widens
      its query instead of concluding the registry is empty.
    </p>

    <h3><code>get_design</code></h3>
    <p>
      Takes a <code>slug</code> and returns that system's DESIGN.md
      <strong>verbatim</strong> — writing the result to disk reproduces the
      registry's file byte for byte. Provenance is already inside the
      frontmatter, so nothing is prepended that would end up committed as part
      of your DESIGN.md.
    </p>
    <p>
      The file is validated before it is returned. The registry cannot serve a
      non-conformant file — the build refuses to produce one — but this is the
      last point before an agent follows the file as though it were sound, so it
      is checked here rather than assumed.
    </p>

    <h2>Asking for it</h2>
    <p>
      Once connected, an ordinary request is enough: <em>"find a dark design
      system with a restrained accent and set this project up with it."</em> The
      agent searches, fetches, writes DESIGN.md, and has the tokens it needs
      before writing any UI.
    </p>

    <p style="margin-top:2rem;">
      Prefer the terminal? <a href="/cli">The CLI</a> does the same job.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
